From 4369546696ddfb6bcedb681e95b32c6320e1d087 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Orsavio P. Delmare" <orsavio@delmare.lu>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:47:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/50] docs: the FIT default config is not a hardware
 statement (ECW230v3 blocker)

Pre-implementation blocker 1 planned to determine the ECW230v3 board by
inspecting which config its stock FIT defaults to. Evidence from a sibling
SKU shows that inference is unsound.

Three ECW336 units were brought up over UART (ECW336-firmware-tools). The
ECW336's FIT also defaults to config@hk08, yet a live unit reports
machid=8010006 -- that is ap-hk07 -- with soc_version_major=2. Conversely a
known-ap-hk07 EWS377-FIT 1.1.65 image defaults to config@hk01.c4. So
configurations/default reflects whatever the vendor's QSDK build selected,
not the silicon. Userspace is no better: the ECW336 prints "Platform Name:
ap-hk01-c6" while its own kernel reports AP-HK07.

What actually decides it is machid -- u-boot matches on it and the embedded
flash.scr gates on machid/soc_hw_version -- with the DTB's qcom,msm-id as the
board discriminator (hk07 = 0x156 0x185, hk08/hk06 = 0x158 0x188).

That turns the ECW230v3 question from "inspect the vendor image and guess"
into one command at the u-boot prompt:

    printenv machid soc_version_major soc_version_minor

DEVICE_DTS_CONFIG should match the board machid reports, not the vendor FIT's
default label. Blocker 1 is rewritten accordingly. Note this settles the
method only -- no ECW230v3 unit has been read here, so the ECW230v3 board
itself remains unverified.
